<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_Warcasket.xml                       Warcasket - WARCASKET_SUIT_CLASS_1

  Owner ruling (WASTELAND_BEDAZZLE_SITTING_1, 2026-09-28), verbatim: "very
  resistant to extreme temps + vacuum + toxins, an alternative to space
  suits and ocean access, but very slow, bulky, prone to failure under
  compound threats - a primitive tank around a person."

  SHAPE cribbed from three precedents already in this codebase (read in
  full before writing this file):
    - RUT_SealedSuit.xml (UtinniPatches) - the ApparelMakeableBase/
      Middle+Shell/ElectricTailoringBench+HandTailoringBench recipe shape.
    - RM_ChillHeatedSuit.xml (DivingInteraction) - real VacuumResistance
      equippedStatOffset usage, and the 2026-09-28 corrected lesson this
      file obeys: ParentName resolves by an XML node's own Name="..."
      attribute, never by <defName>. RM_Warcasket below carries
      Name="RM_Warcasket" for exactly that reason - RM_WarcasketJunker
      inherits from it correctly rather than repeating that bug.
    - RM_ScaldGear.xml (TerminalBiomes) - three distinct protection stats
      legitimately coexisting on one garment (here: Insulation_Cold/Heat,
      VacuumResistance, ToxicEnvironmentResistance, RM_HazardousTerrainProtection),
      each a REAL vanilla or repo-shared stat, not invented flavor:
        Insulation_Cold/Insulation_Heat  -> extreme-temp rated (vanilla)
        VacuumResistance (equippedStatOffset) -> vacuum rated (Odyssey's
          own stat; StatWorker_VacuumResistance)
        ToxicEnvironmentResistance (statBases) -> toxin rated (Biotech's
          own stat; gates HediffComp_ImmunizableToxic and pollution/toxic
          fallout exposure - the same vanilla mechanism a gas mask uses)
        RM_HazardousTerrainProtection -> this mod's own terrain-survival
          stat (RM_WarcasketStats.xml), read by
          RM_MapComponent_HazardousTerrainImmersion.

  MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey" on the ThingDef itself is a LOAD-
  SAFETY guard only (CLAUDE.md: "assume all DLCs" is a design axis, not a
  reason to skip a load-order guard) - VacuumResistance and Room.Vacuum
  are Odyssey-era stat/mechanic and this def's whole "alternative to a
  space suit" framing assumes it is present, same guard RM_ChillHeatedSuit
  already carries.

  COMPOUND-FAILURE MECHANIC: RM_CompProperties_WarcasketIntegrity (see
  RM_CompWarcasketIntegrity.cs). Not flavor text - counts how many of
  {vacuum, extreme temp, toxic terrain} are simultaneously true for the
  wearer right now, and once 2+ stack, rolls a real failure chance every
  check that damages the suit's own HP and injures the wearer with a
  tendable RM_WarcasketBreach hediff. A single hazard alone never fails
  the suit - "a primitive tank" survives one threat fine; it is the
  COMPOUND case that is dangerous, per the ruling's own framing.

  RECIPE: crafted on TableMachining. The sitting's "cask bay" is a
  gravship hazmat hold for waste casks (RM_CaskBay.xml), not a warcasket
  workbench, so no other recipeUser is owed.

  ART: infrastructure/artpipe (registry, done/, _artsrc/) searched for
  "warcasket" before writing this file - nothing found generated or
  ruled on. Queued this pass via fill_queue.py (rimflow_item_id
  WARCASKET_SUIT_CLASS_1) and the artpipe daemon finished both jobs
  (facts PASS) before this file was committed, so graphicData.texPath
  below is the REAL generated icon for each def, copied into this mod's
  own Textures/ - not a placeholder. wornGraphicPath still reuses
  vanilla's real shipped Vacsuit paperdoll (same legitimate move
  RUT_SealedSuit/RM_ChillHeatedSuit/RM_CrackWaxSuit already make in this
  codebase): the generated art is a single flat icon render, not a
  4-facing rigged paperdoll, so it serves the inventory/ground icon while
  the paperdoll still needs a real donor.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ApparelMakeableBase" Name="RM_Warcasket" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RM_Warcasket</defName>
    <label>warcasket</label>
    <description>A crude, riveted shell built to keep a person alive anywhere at once — scavenged plate over rubberized joints, a sealed chest unit doing the work of a space suit, a radiation liner doing the work of a gas mask. It is not elegant. It is not fast. Whoever welded it together was not building armor; they were building a primitive tank to stand inside, and it shows in every over-built seam. It holds against extreme heat, extreme cold, vacuum and poisoned ground all at once — right up until it doesn't, because nothing this improvised holds every seam forever when everything is trying to kill you simultaneously.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/RM_Warcasket/RM_Warcasket</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>1.0</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <!-- RM_CompWarcasketIntegrity overrides CompTickRare; apparel defaults to tickerType Never, so
         without this line the compound-failure roll never ran (Thing.DoTick only ticks Rare/Normal). -->
    <tickerType>Rare</tickerType>
    <tradeability>Sellable</tradeability>
    <costList>
      <Steel>200</Steel>
      <Plasteel>30</Plasteel>
      <ComponentIndustrial>8</ComponentIndustrial>
    </costList>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>320</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToMake>60000</WorkToMake>
      <Mass>32</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.25</Flammability>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.62</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.7</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>140</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>100</Insulation_Heat>
      <RM_HazardousTerrainProtection>0.9</RM_HazardousTerrainProtection>
      <EquipDelay>25</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <!-- "very slow, bulky" - a heavier movement/work penalty than any
           other suit in this codebase (RM_ChillHeatedSuit's -1.25 is the
           previous ceiling); this is the point, not an oversight. -->
      <MoveSpeed>-1.8</MoveSpeed>
      <WorkSpeedGlobal>-0.25</WorkSpeedGlobal>
      <VacuumResistance>0.85</VacuumResistance>
      <!-- pawn stat reads equippedStatOffsets (vanilla gas/tox masks); it was in statBases, which nothing reads -->
      <ToxicEnvironmentResistance>0.9</ToxicEnvironmentResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ApparelArmor</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>HiTechArmor</li>
      <li>Armor</li>
    </tradeTags>
    <smeltable>true</smeltable>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Waist</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/Vacsuit/Vacsuit</wornGraphicPath>
      <layers>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>IndustrialAdvanced</li>
        <li>Vacsuit</li>
      </tags>
      <defaultOutfitTags>
        <li>Worker</li>
        <li>Soldier</li>
      </defaultOutfitTags>
      <useDeflectMetalEffect>true</useDeflectMetalEffect>
      <soundWear>Wear_PowerArmor</soundWear>
      <soundRemove>Remove_PowerArmor</soundRemove>
    </apparel>
    <recipeMaker>
      <recipeUsers>
        <li>TableMachining</li>
      </recipeUsers>
      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
      <effectWorking>Smith</effectWorking>
      <soundWorking>Recipe_Smith</soundWorking>
      <displayPriority>236</displayPriority>
    </recipeMaker>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Warcasket.RM_CompProperties_WarcasketIntegrity">
        <checkIntervalTicks>250</checkIntervalTicks>
        <vacuumThreshold>0.5</vacuumThreshold>
        <extremeColdThresholdC>-60</extremeColdThresholdC>
        <extremeHeatThresholdC>70</extremeHeatThresholdC>
        <baseFailureChancePerCheck>0.015</baseFailureChancePerCheck>
        <failureChancePerExtraHazard>0.02</failureChancePerExtraHazard>
        <integrityDamagePerFailure>12</integrityDamagePerFailure>
        <wearerHediffSeverityPerFailure>0.08</wearerHediffSeverityPerFailure>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       RM_WarcasketJunker — the Junker-adjusted variant. wasteland.md §7:
       "a dead Junker in an adjusted warcasket is a sealed salvage-within-
       salvage: suit, tools, and the half-extracted core still in its
       grips." Sealed at death by RM_CompSarcophagusSeal; cracked open by
       the corpse float-menu job (RM_Sarcophagus.cs), which drops the suit
       and spawns `salvage` below: the welded extraction tooling
       (components + steel) and RM_HalfExtractedCore. generateAllowChance 0: this variant should only ever
       appear via a Junker PawnKindDef's own <apparel> list once that
       exists, never scattered onto random pawns by vanilla's own
       apparel-generation roll.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_Warcasket">
    <defName>RM_WarcasketJunker</defName>
    <label>adjusted warcasket</label>
    <description>A warcasket further modified for the one job Junkers actually do: standing inside a fuel-hot ruin long enough to cut a reactor core loose. Extraction clamps and a hooked prying tool are welded to one forearm; extra fuel-stained canisters ride the chest unit where a soldier's would carry ammunition. Hazard stripes are painted crudely over the plating by hand, again and again, by someone who has already died once in a suit exactly like it.</description>
    <generateAllowChance>0</generateAllowChance>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/RM_WarcasketJunker/RM_WarcasketJunker</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>1.0</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Warcasket.RM_JunkerSarcophagusExtension">
        <isSealedSarcophagus>true</isSealedSarcophagus>
        <flavorNote>A dead Junker, sealed. Whatever they were hauling out is still in here with them.</flavorNote>
        <crackOpenTicks>1200</crackOpenTicks>
        <salvage>
          <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
          <Steel>25</Steel>
          <RM_HalfExtractedCore>1</RM_HalfExtractedCore>
        </salvage>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Warcasket.RM_CompProperties_SarcophagusSeal" />
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
